{Time limit 45 moves in 2 hr 30' then 18 per hr} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4
4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. f4 Nc6 ({Later in the tournament Ayriss played} 6...
Bg7 {in this position and drew.}) 7. Nxc6 bxc6 {[3']} 8. e5 Bg4 {[23']} ({
The usual move is} 8... Nd7 {but 8...Bg4 doesn't seem bad.}) 9. Be2 Bxe2 10.
Qxe2 dxe5 11. fxe5 {[9']} (11. Qxe5 {is too rash after} Bg7) 11... Nd5 (11...
Nd7 $1 12. e6) 12. Nxd5 ({After much thought. I can't let him double my QS
Pawns. Also my e-Pawn is weak after....Bg7 & .....Qc7 or ......Qa5} 12. Bd2 Qb6
{isn't too happy.}) 12... cxd5 13. e6 fxe6 {Forced in view if 14.Qb5+} 14. Qxe6
Qd7 {A good move. If I exchange queens I am left with a bad endgame.} 15. Qe2 (
15. Qe5 $142) 15... Bg7 16. O-O Rf8 17. c3 ({Prevents 17...d5 and strengthens
my weak QS somewhat.} 17. Rxf8+ {Favours Black}) 17... Rxf1+ 18. Qxf1 e5 {
Now Black has all the chances.} 19. Qe2 Kf8 20. Be3 Kg8 21. Rd1 {Threatens 22.
Qd3 winning the d-Pawn.} Qb7 22. Qf3 Rd8 (22... e4 {is bad.}) 23. h3 Rd7 {[95']
} 24. Qf2 {[88']} d4 $1 {Securing a passed pawn.} 25. cxd4 exd4 {[99']} 26. Bg5
{[100']} ({Not} 26. Bxd4 $4 Qd5) 26... h6 27. Bc1 d3 28. Qf3 Qxf3 {Made by the
dictates of the clock.} (28... Qb4 {keeping the Queens on seems to offer him
more chances.}) 29. gxf3 Rc7 30. Be3 Rd7 {We were both short of time at the
end. A.Ayriss came 48th with 3.5pts. [A.Ayriss came 9= last year (= with
Saemisch!) Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean Parker, 19
December 2022.} 1/2-1/2

