{I now had a half out of two so I was due an easy opponent. I sat down
opposite Michael Basman. Michael is an I.M. who has played top board for
England. Time limit 45 moves in 2 hr 30' then 18 per hr.} 1. c4 e6 2. g3 Nf6 3.
Bg2 d5 4. d4 {[5']} dxc4 {[20']} 5. Qa4+ Bd7 6. Qxc4 Bc6 7. Nf3 Nbd7 8. Nc3 Be7
9. O-O O-O 10. a3 {[19']} Ne4 {[66'] Black must prevent e4} 11. b4 {Gaining
space.} Nb6 12. Qd3 Nxc3 13. Qxc3 {[28']} Bf6 {[85']} 14. e3 {[31']} Na4 {
[90'] This seems wrong as the Knight serves no purpose on a4 and merely serves
as a target for attack.} 15. Qc2 Qd6 {Hoping to play ...e5.} 16. Rb1 {
Threatening the knight by 17 b5.} Bb5 {[95']} 17. Re1 {[43']} Rfd8 (17... e5 {
Loses the b-Pawn.}) 18. Nd2 $1 {Very strong, attacking the b-Pawn also
threatening to place the Knight at e4 or c5.} e5 $6 {Leading to greater
complications.} 19. Bxb7 exd4 $6 ({Now the game goes mad.} 19... Rab8 20. Ne4
Qb6 21. Nxf6+ Qxf6 22. dxe5 Qxe5 23. Be4 {and if} Nc3 24. Bb2) 20. Ne4 {
A useful zwischenzug.} d3 {A fantastic position.} 21. Qb3 Qe7 22. Bxa8 Rxa8 {
[116']} 23. Qd5 {[86']} c6 24. Nxf6+ ({If} 24. Qf5 Be5) 24... Qxf6 25. Qd4 $5 {
This gives up a Pawn in order to minimise Black's counterplay.} ({e.g.} 25. Qb3
Qc3 {followed by ...c5 and ...Bc6.} (25... Nc3 {would also be strong})) 25...
Qxd4 26. exd4 Nc3 27. Rb2 Ne2+ 28. Kg2 Nxd4 {I realised here that Black has
acquired winning chances and White's game is very difficult due to the
ineffectiveness of his pieces.} 29. Re7 {Black refused a draw here. The threat
was ...Nc2 and ...Nxa3.} Kf8 30. Re4 {Making life very difficult.} c5 $1 {
I now had to think for a very long time. Black threatens ...Bc6.} 31. Rh4 $1 ({
The only chance. I considered} 31. bxc5 $4 Bc6 32. f3 {but it's not good
enough.}) ({If the rook moves off the 4th, e.g.} 31. Re3 {Black plays} c4) ({If
} 31. Rf4 Ne2) 31... Ne2 32. Rxh7 {I offered a draw which he refused.} Kg8 {
He offered a draw which I refused!!} (32... Nxc1 33. Rh8+ {is too good for
White.}) 33. Rh5 $1 Bc6+ ({If now...} 33... Nxc1 34. Rxc5 d2 35. Rxd2 Nb3) 34.
Kf1 Nxc1 35. Rxc5 Rc8 {I refused a draw here.} 36. Rxc1 Bg2+ 37. Kxg2 Rxc1 38.
Rd2 Rc3 39. a4 Ra3 40. b5 Kf8 41. Kf3 Ke7 42. Ke3 Rxa4 43. Rxd3 Rb4 {My only
hope of a win is too keep pawns on both sides.} 44. Ra3 Rxb5 45. Rxa7+ {[149']}
Ke6 {The game is a dead draw but I played on in the hope Black might make a
mistake.} 46. Ra3 g6 47. f4 Rb2 48. h4 Kf5 49. Kf3 Rb5 (49... Rb7 $2 50. Ra5+
Kf6 51. Kg4) 50. Re3 Kf6 51. Kg4 Ra5 52. Rb3 Rc5 53. Rb6+ Kg7 54. Rb1 Kf6 55.
Rh1 Rh5 56. Kf3 Ra5 57. Re1 Rb5 58. g4 Ra5 59. Re3 Rb5 60. Ra3 Kg7 61. g5 Rc5
62. Kg4 Rc4 63. Rf3 Ra4 64. Kg3 f6 65. f5 gxf5 ({Not} 65... fxg5 $2 66. f6+ {
Very complicated. My play was rather uneven and too hasty in places. M.J.
Basman came =11-17th with 6.5pts. I did have more luck against Michael in a
league match in Dec '64. Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean
Parker, 19 December 2022.}) 1/2-1/2

