{Time limit 45 moves in 2 hr 30' then 18 per hr} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5
4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 c5 7. d5 {Unusual. It has the disadvantage of
weakening him on the long diagonal.} Bg7 8. Qc2 O-O 9. Ne2 e6 10. Nf4 exd5 11.
Nxd5 {White has a strong square at d5, but he has pawn weaknesses and Black
has the better development.} Re8 {Threatening 12...Qxd5.} 12. Bc4 Nc6 13. O-O
Be6 14. Rb1 {[40']} b6 {[20']} 15. Rd1 {White has slightly the better of it
now.} Bxd5 16. Bxd5 Qc7 17. g3 (17. Bf4 Be5) 17... Rac8 18. f4 {Now White has
much the better of it, with his impressive centre and strong bishop at d5.} Ne7
{[30']} 19. Bc4 {[60']} ({If} 19. c4 {I can get some play by} Nc6 {and ...Nd4.}
) 19... Nc6 20. Be3 Kh8 21. Bd5 Ne7 22. Bf2 (22. Bxf7 Nf5) 22... Nxd5 23. exd5
(23. Rxd5 $142 {followed by 24 Rbd1.}) 23... c4 $1 {Isolating the d-pawn.} 24.
Bd4 Qd7 25. Bxg7+ {[95']} Kxg7 26. Qd2 Red8 {[60']} 27. Qd4+ Kg8 28. Rd2 {
Or else he loses the d-pawn} Qd6 29. Qe5 Qc5+ 30. Kg2 (30. Qd4 $2 Rxd5 $1)
30... Qd6 31. Qxd6 $2 {After this exchange his d-pawn is doomed.} Rxd6 32. Kf3
Kf8 33. Ke4 Ke7 34. Kf3 Rd7 35. Ke4 Rc5 {Prevents 36 Kd4} 36. Rbd1 Kd6 37. Kf3
Rc8 38. Rd4 Kc5 39. f5 {Desperation.} gxf5 40. Kf4 Rcd8 {[Adjourned]} 41. Ke5 {
[Sealed move]} (41. Kxf5 $2 {Black queens first and wins, but everything else
loses as well.}) 41... Re8+ 42. Kxf5 Re3 43. Re4 Rxc3 44. Re5 Rd3 {M.J.
Lavender came =42nd - 47th with 4pts. Source: Dick Collins scorebook,
contributed by Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.} 0-1

