{Time limit 45 moves in 2 hr 30' then 18 per hr} 1. e4 e6 2. d3 {The best
method if one wishes to avoid the French.} d5 3. Nd2 c5 4. g3 g6 5. Bg2 Bg7 6.
Ngf3 Nc6 7. c3 Nge7 8. Qe2 {In view of Black's next move this doesn't seem too
good.} e5 9. O-O O-O 10. Re1 {White's e-file pressure comes to nothing.} h6 11.
h3 Kh7 12. Nf1 Be6 13. Bd2 Qd7 14. Kh2 f5 {Black now has much the better of it,
Whites manoeuvering being much too slow.} 15. exf5 Bxf5 16. g4 Be6 (16... Bxg4
{isn't quite sound at the moment.}) 17. Ng3 Rf7 18. Rf1 Raf8 {Now sacrifices
on g4 & f3 are in the air.} 19. Rae1 Ng8 $2 {Careless. I was thinking that
White couldn't do much I intended to move the Knight to f6 and sacrifice on g4.
} 20. g5 $1 h5 $2 {Losing at least a pawn. I saw the coming sacrifice but for
some reason thought it was unsound.} 21. Nxh5 $1 Rxf3 $5 ({I now realised that
} 21... gxh5 {loses to} 22. Nh4 $1 {I thought about playing on a pawn down 
(which seems best) but decided to try and force something by complicating
matters. An unfortunate decision.}) 22. Bxf3 ({If} 22. Nxg7 Rxh3+ $1 23. Bxh3
Bxh3 {and White's knight is stuck.}) 22... gxh5 23. Bxh5 Bxh3 {This loses but
there seems little alternative.} 24. Rh1 Nge7 {If the bishop moves I can't
survive the coming discovered check.} 25. Kg3 $1 e4 ({The move I had
originally intended,} 25... Nf5+ {, doesn't work.}) 26. Rxh3 Kg8 27. dxe4 dxe4
28. Qc4+ Nd5 29. Rxe4 Qf5 30. f4 b5 31. Qe2 {C.A.S.Damant came 18th - 23rd
with 6pts. Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean Parker, 19
December 2022.} 1-0

