{Time limit 45 moves in 2 hr 30' then 18 per hr} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6
4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 O-O $2 {A rather common error (According to
Alekhine)} 7. Bxc6 dxc6 (7... bxc6 {may be better.}) 8. Nxe5 Bd6 {This move
has the disadvantage of allowing me to threaten a fork after 9 Nf3.} 9. Nf3 Bg4
$2 {Giving up a piece for an almost non-existent attack.} 10. e5 Re8 11. exd6
Qxd6 12. d3 Rxe1+ 13. Qxe1 Bxf3 14. gxf3 Re8 {Black's only hope is that I will
have difficulty developing my QS.} 15. Be3 Nh5 16. Nc3 Qg6+ 17. Kh1 Qf5 18. Qg1
Re6 (18... Qxf3+ 19. Qg2 Qf5 20. Rg1 {wins a pawn but loses a tempo.}) 19. Qg4
{[26']} Qa5 {Now Black has a rook which is pinned, a knight which needs
protecting by the queen, and a queen which is out of play.} 20. Rg1 h6 21. Qh3
({Better than} 21. Qh4 Qf5) 21... Kh7 22. Rg4 Nf6 23. Rf4 {Intending 24 Qf5+.}
b5 ({Not} 23... Re5 24. Ra4 $1) 24. a3 c5 25. Qf5+ Kg8 (25... Kh8 26. Qxc5) 26.
Qxc5 c6 27. Ra4 Qc7 28. Rxa6 Nd7 29. Ra7 Qd8 {Now he loses a piece but it was
all over anyway.} 30. Qd4 Re7 31. Ne4 {J.D.Barham came = 42nd - 47th with 4pts.
Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.}
1-0

