{Time limit 45 moves in 2 hr 30' then 18 per hr} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. Nbd2 d5
4. e3 c5 5. c3 Nc6 6. Bd3 Bd6 7. O-O e5 {A move which leads to great
complications but equalises, I think.} 8. e4 O-O ({To exchange in the centre
is all to White's advantage, e.g.} 8... cxd4 9. cxd4 exd4 10. exd5 Nxd5 11. Nc4
{with a huge lead in development.}) 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. dxc5 Bxc5 11. Ne4 Be7 ({
It was vital to cover g5.} 11... Bb6 $4 12. Nfg5 {leaves me in a hopeless mess.
}) 12. Nfg5 Bf5 ({The alternative} 12... f5 $6 13. Qh5 h6 14. Bc4 $1 hxg5 15.
Bxg5 $3) 13. Qf3 {The sight of the above variations must have dazzled White.}
Bg6 14. Qh3 $2 {And this loses outright. White still had visions of a grand
attack.} h6 {[42']} 15. Nf3 {[77']} ({No better is} 15. c4 Nf4) 15... f5 16.
Bxh6 {The only chance.} fxe4 {Rarely does one reach a position after 16 moves
where one is a piece down with 3 others en prise.} 17. Bc4 exf3 18. Rfd1 Bf7
19. Bxg7 Kxg7 20. Qg3+ Bg6 ({I must give up a piece. Not} 20... Bg5 21. h4) 21.
Rxd5 Bd6 22. Rad1 ({Slightly better was} 22. h4 {but it's all the same in the
end.}) 22... Rf6 23. h4 Kh8 24. Qg5 Bf7 25. h5 Bxd5 26. Bxd5 Qf8 27. Bxf3 Qg7
28. Qe3 Raf8 {D.B.Pennycuick came = 24th - 31st with 5.5pts. Source: Dick
Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.} 0-1

