{Time limit 45 moves in 2 hr 30' then 18 per hr} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4
4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. f4 Nc6 7. Be3 Bg7 8. Qd2 O-O 9. Bc4 Nxd4 10. Bxd4 Be6
11. Bd5 Qa5 ({11 Bd5 was a bit odd, based on the variation} 11... Bxd5 12. Nxd5
Nxd5 13. Bxg7 Kxg7 14. Qxd5 {with some advantage.}) 12. Bxe6 fxe6 13. O-O-O e5
$2 {This seems wrong.} 14. fxe5 dxe5 15. Be3 b5 16. Kb1 b4 17. Nd5 Nxe4 18.
Nxe7+ ({Unfortunately} 18. Qxb4 Qxb4 19. Nxb4 Nf2 {seems too good for Black.})
18... Kh8 19. Qe1 $2 {As I played this (which threatens 20 Nxg6+) I saw
Black's reply.} Nc3+ $1 {[83']} 20. bxc3 bxc3 21. Ka1 Qb4 22. Nxg6+ ({Not} 22.
Rb1 Qxe7 23. Qxc3 $2 {opening the long black diagonal.}) 22... hxg6 23. Rb1 Qc4
24. Rb7 Rab8 ({Not} 24... Qe4 $4 25. Rxg7 $1) 25. Rxa7 Rb2 26. Qc1 Rfb8 $2 {
[111']} ({Missing the win. Correct is} 26... Rf7 27. Ra5 Qe2 {, etc.}) 27. Bh6
$1 {[59'] Forcing the draw.} R8b7 (27... Rb1+ $4 28. Qxb1 Rxb1+ 29. Rxb1 {
wins 2 Rs & B for the Q.}) (27... Bf6 {is no better:} 28. Bf8 $1) 28. Bxg7+
Kxg7 (28... Kxg7 29. Rxb7+ Rxb7 {and the position at the end seems good for
Black, e.g.} 30. Qe3 e4 31. Rb1 Rxb1+ 32. Kxb1 Qf1+ 33. Qc1 Qxg2 34. Qe1 Qd2 $1
35. Qg1 e3 $3) 29. Rxb7+ Rxb7 {P.Dean came = 11 - 17th with 6.5 pts. Source:
Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.} 1/2-1/2

