{Time limit 45 moves in 2 hr 30' then 18 per hr} 1. c4 Nf6 2. Nc3 g6 3. e4 d6
4. d4 Bg7 5. Be2 O-O 6. Bg5 h6 7. Be3 e5 {A.K.May seemed to think this was
wrong.} 8. d5 c6 9. h3 cxd5 10. cxd5 Ne8 {Deciding to meet his attack half-way}
11. g4 {He said he played this to avoid 11...f5......!!} f5 {Nevertheless.} 12.
f3 {Exchanging is to Black's advantage.} f4 $2 ({The blocking off of the KS
leaves me with a hopeless game. I had expected to hold my own on the QS but
was disilusioned. Best, I think, was} 12... Na6) 13. Bf2 a6 14. a4 Qa5 15. Bc4
Nd7 16. Nge2 Qb4 {Doubtful but what else is there? Best is just to do nothing
but it's pretty hopeless.} 17. b3 Nc5 18. O-O a5 $4 {As soon as I played this
I realised my mistake. I played this in order to prevent b4 after Na2.} 19. Nb5
{I had intended to meet this with 19...Bd7 but had missed 20 Be1.} Na6 (19...
Bd7 20. Be1) 20. Nc1 {Once again my old trouble of playing too quickly. Alan K.
May came = 18 - 23rd with 6pts. Source: Dick Collins scorebook, contributed by
Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.} 1-0

