{"CHESS by Leonard Barden: In the Southern Counties championship at Bognor
earlier this year, the 17-year-old Yugo­slav V. Musil (Black, to move)
reached this position against the former Sussex champion, W. A. Wlnser. How
should Black continue, and with what result? Par solving times: 20 seconds,
master or expert; 3 minutes, county strength: 5 minutes; club strength, 8
minutes, above average; 12 minutes, average." No solution found in the
newspaper but, assuming that Black actually found the answer, it must
presumably have been} 1... c3 2. bxc3 Re3 {and wins. Source: Birmingham
Evening Mail and Despatch, 31 Aug 1963, p9. Contributed by Ulrich Tamm, 26
December 2022.} 0-1

