{Time limit 45 moves in 2 hr 30' then 18 per hr} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. g3 f5
4. Bg2 Nf6 5. e4 {I was not willing to let Black set up a strong centre and
this move seems the best way of keeping the initiative. Also, I have a strong
square at d5.} d6 ({I had expected Black to try and restrain my d-pawn with} 
5... Bc5) 6. Nge2 Be6 {[34']} ({Black would do better to go into a sort of
Leningrad with} 6... g6) 7. b3 Be7 8. d4 {[8']} Nxd4 {If he doesn't exchange
he gets a hopeless game by 9 d5.} 9. Nxd4 exd4 10. Qxd4 fxe4 11. Nxe4 O-O {
[74']} 12. O-O {[20']} (12. Bb2 {is the alternative.}) 12... Nxe4 {[99'] Black,
of course, must free his position. This move exchanges off my strong knight
and gives his bishop some scope.} 13. Qxe4 Bc8 {[109']} ({Black's position was
very difficult. More chances, it seems, were offered by the pawn sacrifice} 
13... Qd7 {(which Black had considered), for then Black's bishops get a lot of
play and my pieces, which are undeveloped, may prove weak.} 14. Qxb7 Bf6 15.
Rb1 Bf5 {is quite good for Black.}) 14. Bf4 $1 {By far the best square for the
bishop as becomes apparent in a few moves.} Rb8 {Black has nothing better than
this roundabout way of developing his QS.} 15. Rfe1 Bf6 ({Not} 15... Re8 $4 16.
Bg5) 16. Rad1 {[33'] White has an ideal position where each piece is in its
most effective position. Black's position was positionally lost several moves
ago.} Bd7 {[112']} ({Black has no constructive moves.} 16... Bg4 {was the only
hope.}) 17. c5 $1 {[35'] Now it's all over.} Re8 {[122']} 18. Qd5+ Kh8 19. cxd6
cxd6 {[129']} ({The move on which Black may have been relying.} 19... Bc6 {
fails against.} 20. dxc7 $1) 20. Qxd6 Rxe1+ 21. Rxe1 Rc8 {[135']} 22. Bxb7 {
[45']} Bh3 {[141']} 23. Bxc8 Qxc8 {[141']} 24. Qb8 {[45'] (Black would have to
make his next 22 moves in 9 minutes) M.J.Dymond came = 24th - 31st with 5.5pts.
A very good game. White's game won itself from the position after 14 moves.
This was my best game of the tournament. I came 18 - 23rd with 6pts. The
winner was Nikola Karaklajic with 9pts. Source: Dick Collins scorebook,
contributed by Sean Parker, 19 December 2022.} 1-0

